# Customer vs Tailor (team member)

Harewa has two distinct product surfaces. Do not merge them, and do not copy TailorsMate’s mixed bottom nav (Home / Tailors / Discover / Chat) into either section.

Use Harewa UI (gold `#D4AF37`, stone/gray, existing layouts). Borrow structure and workflows from reference screenshots, not branding.

## Customers (`client` preset)

Stay in public storefront + `/profile`:

- Shop, cart, checkout, customize
- Find a Tailor (`/tailors`) — discovery and booking only
- Profile: orders, customizations, measurements, tailoring jobs (as customer), wishlist, info
- Campaign **join** as a participant: `/join/[slug]` then submit measurements from `/profile?tab=measurements`

Never put tailor studio tools (client roster, campaign CRUD, sponsored credits) on customer pages.

## Tailors / team members (`tailor` Membership preset)

Stay under `/tailor/*` only:

- `/tailor/home` — studio dashboard + **their** client roster
- `/tailor/jobs` — jobs/appointments for work assigned to them
- `/tailor/campaigns` — measurement campaigns they own
- `/tailor/notifications` — tailor alerts
- `/tailor/dashboard` — studio profile / portfolio editor

Default after sign-in: `/tailor/home`. Header “Store” may open `/home` so they can shop; that is the only intended cross-nav.

## Do not

- Link tailor nav to `/profile`, `/tailors`, or `/trending-fashion` as primary workspace items
- Put customer orders/wishlist inside the tailor dashboard
- Weaken RBAC so customers can manage tailor clients or campaigns
